WEBVTT

00:01:00.015 --> 00:01:01.682
So we've been eating, drinking,

00:01:01.706 --> 00:01:03.976
thinking, living public space

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.947
for quite a long time.

00:01:05.971 --> 00:01:08.216
And it's taught us really one thing,

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.184
and that is to truly
make good public space,

00:01:12.208 --> 00:01:15.434
you have to erase the distinctions

00:01:15.458 --> 00:01:18.059
between architecture, urbanism,

00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:19.934
landscape, media design

00:01:19.958 --> 00:01:21.518
and so on.

00:01:21.542 --> 00:01:23.547
It really goes beyond distinction.

00:01:23.571 --> 00:01:26.601
Now we're moving onto Washington, D.C.

00:01:26.625 --> 00:01:28.934
and we're working
on another transformation,

00:01:28.958 --> 00:01:31.559
and that is for the existing
Hirshhorn Museum